# Clock in (LLP 1125 D9): a sequence that follows `clk` waits; ticks at 125
# give it a tempo; Start counts in two beats and plays; a tempo change to 100
# re-anchors (a tick a delivery, so hits are taken back by `clock`); a gap
# starts the window over; Stop leaves it waiting (heard by the handler); Song
# Position and Continue resume at beat 4; a key restart waits again; the
# gate stops it, and it answers as an internal clock again.
prefer midi.outputs synth midi.inputs clk
tap ask
tap start
midi clk clock 125 1000
midi clk fa
midi clk clock 125 2000
midi clk clock 100 1000
clock +25
midi clk f8
clock +25
midi clk f8
clock +25
midi clk f8
clock +700
midi clk clock 100 400
midi clk fc
midi clk f2 10 00
midi clk fb
midi clk clock 100 1000
tap restart
midi clk clock 100 200
midi clk fa
midi clk clock 100 300
# Start again, then ticks 10 ms apart: each re-anchor keeps what the last
# one kept, and a note at the hold's edge is neither taken back nor queued
# again (review round 1). Start again exactly at the count-in's first hit
# takes it back; after a gap no beat played is played again (round 2).
midi clk fa
clock +25
midi clk fa
clock +10
midi clk f8
clock +10
midi clk f8
clock +30
midi clk f8
clock +1500
midi clk f8
clock +10
midi clk f8
clock +200
tap stop
clock +500
